    {
      "id": "75582a54059d0bc4e1da5cf4f73a4d323057a064",
      "individual_note": false,
      "resolvable": true,
      "resolved": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 616791211,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "This change now causes some warnings to be generated:\n\n    libmaxminddb.lib(maxminddb.c.obj) : warning LNK4291: module may contain '__except' (Structured Exception Handling) but was not compiled with /guard:ehcont; generating conservative metadata [C:\\builds\\wireshark\\wireshark\\build\\mmdbresolve.vcxproj]\n    libmaxminddb.lib(data-pool.c.obj) : warning LNK4291: module may contain '__except' (Structured Exception Handling) but was not compiled with /guard:ehcont; generating conservative metadata [C:\\builds\\wireshark\\wireshark\\build\\mmdbresolve.vcxproj]\n    minizip.lib(unzip.c.obj) : warning LNK4291: module may contain '__except' (Structured Exception Handling) but was not compiled with /guard:ehcont; generating conservative metadata [C:\\builds\\wireshark\\wireshark\\build\\wireshark.vcxproj]\n    minizip.lib(zip.c.obj) : warning LNK4291: module may contain '__except' (Structured Exception Handling) but was not compiled with /guard:ehcont; generating conservative metadata [C:\\builds\\wireshark\\wireshark\\build\\wireshark.vcxproj]\n    qtmain.lib(qtmain_win.obj) : warning LNK4291: module may contain '__except' (Structured Exception Handling) but was not compiled with /guard:ehcont; generating conservative metadata [C:\\builds\\wireshark\\wireshark\\build\\wireshark.vcxproj]\n\nI don't know if these need to be treated or suppressed.",
          "author": {
            "id": 6621762,
            "username": "graham.bloice",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Graham Bloice",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/8730bfac2267cb97ff1f8187d285f244745a03a783055c8fd6fcd679bfa71c6e?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/graham.bloice"
          },
          "created_at": "2021-07-01T17:39:54.863Z",
          "updated_at": "2021-07-01T18:38:34.429Z",
          "system": false,
          "noteable_id": 103975098,
          "noteable_type": "MergeRequest",
          "project_id": 7898047,
          "resolvable": true,
          "resolved": false,
          "resolved_by": null,
          "resolved_at": null,
          "confidential": false,
          "internal": false,
          "imported": false,
          "imported_from": "none",
          "noteable_iid": 3329,
          "commands_changes": {}
        },
        {
          "id": 616825528,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "From the Microsoft page, it seems like adding the flag to the other objects\ncompilation commands would solve the issue.\n\nMoshe",
          "author": {
            "id": 3194989,
            "username": "moshekaplan",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Moshe Kaplan",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://gitlab.com/uploads/-/system/user/avatar/3194989/avatar.png?v=1789950604",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/moshekaplan"
          },
          "created_at": "2021-07-01T18:38:34.374Z",
          "updated_at": "2021-07-01T18:38:34.374Z",
          "system": false,
          "noteable_id": 103975098,
          "noteable_type": "MergeRequest",
          "project_id": 7898047,
          "resolvable": true,
          "resolved": false,
          "resolved_by": null,
          "resolved_at": null,
          "confidential": false,
          "internal": false,
          "imported": false,
          "imported_from": "none",
          "noteable_iid": 3329,
          "commands_changes": {}
        },
        {
          "id": 616929843,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "Given that those are pre complied third party libraries that are not necessarily built with the same MSVC version, this will not help.",
          "author": {
            "id": 6722527,
            "username": "pquantin",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Pascal Quantin",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/9bf49edc6acae0eca821eb90309381794fb4fbea4f3fb7c2378428862ddbb430?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/pquantin"
          },
          "created_at": "2021-07-01T22:45:34.748Z",
          "updated_at": "2021-07-01T22:45:34.748Z",
          "system": false,
          "noteable_id": 103975098,
          "noteable_type": "MergeRequest",
          "project_id": 7898047,
          "resolvable": true,
          "resolved": false,
          "resolved_by": null,
          "resolved_at": null,
          "confidential": false,
          "internal": false,
          "imported": false,
          "imported_from": "none",
          "noteable_iid": 3329,
          "commands_changes": {}
        },
        {
          "id": 616965519,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "Then the only other option would be to ignore the warning.\n\nPer https://docs.microsoft.com/en-us/cpp/build/reference/guard-enable-eh-continuation-metadata?view=msvc-160 :\n> For SEH section info found in COMDATs, but not compiled using /guard:ehcont, the linker emits warning LNK4291. In this case, the linker generates correct but conservative metadata for the section. To ignore this warning, use /IGNORE (Ignore Specific Warnings).",
          "author": {
            "id": 3194989,
            "username": "moshekaplan",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Moshe Kaplan",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://gitlab.com/uploads/-/system/user/avatar/3194989/avatar.png?v=1789950604",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/moshekaplan"
          },
          "created_at": "2021-07-02T00:56:38.631Z",
          "updated_at": "2021-07-02T00:56:38.631Z",
          "system": false,
          "noteable_id": 103975098,
          "noteable_type": "MergeRequest",
          "project_id": 7898047,
          "resolvable": true,
          "resolved": false,
          "resolved_by": null,
          "resolved_at": null,
          "confidential": false,
          "internal": false,
          "imported": false,
          "imported_from": "none",
          "noteable_iid": 3329,
          "commands_changes": {}
        },
        {
          "id": 617756704,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "Myself and several others have noted that this change seems to break incremental rebuilds, see the mail list [here](https://www.wireshark.org/lists/wireshark-dev/202107/msg00000.html) and [here](https://www.wireshark.org/lists/wireshark-dev/202107/msg00006.html).",
          "author": {
            "id": 6621762,
            "username": "graham.bloice",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Graham Bloice",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/8730bfac2267cb97ff1f8187d285f244745a03a783055c8fd6fcd679bfa71c6e?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/graham.bloice"
          },
          "created_at": "2021-07-02T17:25:20.044Z",
          "updated_at": "2021-07-02T17:25:29.544Z",
